and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]

Nothing yet.

## [0.1.0] - 2026-08-07

Initial public release, renamed from `dirscan` to **Treeport**.

### Added

- Tree view of a directory with per-folder totals, item counts, and per-type icons.
- Summary report: totals, breakdown by category and extension, largest files,
  largest directories, oldest/newest files, empty files/dirs, hidden entries,
  symlinks, and max scan depth.
- Full Unicode / right-to-left script support (Persian, Arabic, Hebrew, etc.):
  - Correct UTF-8 handling throughout scanning, sorting, filtering, and export.
  - Automatic UTF-8 console code page switch on Windows (`cmd.exe`/PowerShell),
    fixing Persian/Arabic text rendering as `?`/mojibake.
  - Unicode directional isolates around right-to-left names in the tree,
    tables, and Markdown output, preventing bidi corruption of the
    surrounding ASCII structure.
  - `--utf8-bom` flag for `.txt`/`.md` exports, so older Windows apps
    (Notepad, Excel's plain "open") correctly detect UTF-8 instead of
    guessing the system code page.
- Export formats:
  - `-m, --markdown <file>` — formatted Markdown report.
  - `-j, --json <file>` — structured JSON report for scripts/dashboards/CI
    (never BOM-prefixed, per the JSON spec).
  - `-c, --csv <file>` — flat CSV of every entry (always BOM-prefixed, for
    correct Excel rendering of non-Latin text).
  - `-o, --output <file>` — full detailed per-entry table.
- Duplicate file detection (`--find-duplicates`) by content, grouped and
  sized by wasted disk space.
- Filtering options:
  - `-e, --exclude <name>` — exact-name exclude (repeatable).
  - `--exclude-glob <pattern>` — `*`/`?` wildcard exclude (repeatable).
  - `--include-ext` / `--exclude-ext <ext>` — extension filters (repeatable).
  - `--newer-than` / `--older-than <YYYY-MM-DD>` — modification-date filters.
  - `--min-size <SIZE>` — hide small files from the tree view.
  - `-d, --max-depth <N>` — limit recursion depth.
  - `.treeportignore` — a simple, `.gitignore`-style ignore file auto-loaded
    from the scan root (`--ignore-file` / `--no-ignore-file` to override).
- Live, throttled scan-progress indicator on stderr for large trees
  (`--no-progress` to disable), never touching the actual report output.
- `-t, --top <N>` largest-files/largest-directories count, `-s, --sort
<name|size>` tree sort order, `--ascii` plain-ASCII tree characters,
  `--no-color`/`--color`, `-q, --quiet`, `-f, --full`.
- Cross-platform: Linux, macOS, and Windows, with symlinks detected and
  never followed (safe against cyclic symlinks) and per-entry permission
  errors reported inline instead of aborting the scan.
- Zero external dependencies — pure Rust standard library.

